Negative control for the auth target's params leaving the page url (`S11`/`S18`).

Adopts the router's own instruction to the overlay — `as`, `mode`, `cancelUrl`,
`fresh` — into the surface bag on a page change, so a resolved overlay leaves
`?as=user&fresh=<nonce>` sitting on the page it handed back, and the link a
colleague is sent re-opens the ADD-SESSION journey they never asked for.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the url-state spec — the bag drops every auth target param on a page change.

